# Python / FastAPI
- Inspect actual Python/FastAPI/Pydantic/ORM/package-manager versions first; do not assume APIs.
- Follow existing typing, linting, formatting, DI and module-layout conventions.
- Keep route handlers thin when service/domain layers exist; preserve request/response contracts and status/error semantics.
- Validate external inputs and use structured error handling; do not leak stack traces/secrets.
- Preserve async correctness; avoid blocking work directly in async request paths without a suitable strategy.
- Reuse established DB/session dependencies and lifecycle hooks; avoid ad-hoc globals.
- Avoid import-time side effects and hidden network/database work unless intentionally architectural.
- Use established configuration/environment mechanisms; never hard-code production secrets.
- Keep migrations separate from ordinary application startup unless intentionally coupled.
- Add/update targeted tests for validation, services, API contracts and failure paths; use real repository commands only.
